// Endpoint latency by operation name.
//
// Saved in the workspace as the function EndpointLatency(window) -- see
// docs/day5-appinsights-submission.md for the save steps. The parameter is
// the only change from the exercise's query text: a hardcoded ago(30m)
// makes a function that can only ever answer one question, and the whole
// point of saving it is to re-use it over a different window later.
//
// duration is in MILLISECONDS in the requests table.
//
// count() rather than sum(itemCount) is correct only while sampling is off
// (the Azure Monitor distro defaults to SamplingRatio 1.0, and nothing in
// this app changes it). If sampling is ever enabled, count() reports the
// number of records STORED, not the number of requests that happened, and
// every number in this table silently under-reports.
requests
| where timestamp > ago(window)
| summarize count(), p50=percentile(duration, 50), p99=percentile(duration, 99) by name
| order by p99 desc

// Same query, excluding the Container Apps health probes. The liveness and
// readiness probes run every 10 seconds against /health/live and
// /health/ready (infra/resources.bicep), so on a low-traffic app they are
// the overwhelming majority of rows and bury the endpoints actually being
// measured. Useful as a second saved function, or inline:
//
// requests
// | where timestamp > ago(window)
// | where name !startswith "GET /health"
// | summarize count(), p50=percentile(duration, 50), p99=percentile(duration, 99) by name
// | order by p99 desc
